<title>CANADA: MFP to buy back up to five pct of shares.</title>
<headline>MFP to buy back up to five pct of shares.</headline>
<dateline>MISSISSAUGA, Ontario 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>MFP Technology Services Ltd said on Wednesday it intends to buy back up to 542,607 of its shares, or five percent of the 10,852,149 common shares outstanding, if the price is considered advantageous.</p>
<p>Last year, MFP purchased 211,800 common shares at an average price per share of C$6.18, MFP said.</p>
<p>The company also said its board of directors, at the company's annual meeting today, appointed John McGrath as chairman of the board and elected William Young as a director of MFP.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau  (416) 941-8100</p>
</text>
